.Dd November 15, 2026
.Dt WLPROBE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm wlprobe
.Nd check the shared-memory primitives that Wayland needs
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility checks, one step at a time, the shared-memory path that a
Wayland client uses to hand its pixels to the compositor.
If a step breaks, the output shows which one.
.Nm
takes no arguments.
.Pp
It checks, in order, that:
.Bl -enum
.It
.Xr shm_open 3
creates a new object with
.Dv O_CREAT
and
.Dv O_EXCL .
.It
.Xr ftruncate 2
sets its size to 4096 bytes, and
.Xr fstat 2
reports that size.
.It
The object can be mapped with
.Dv MAP_SHARED
and
.Dv PROT_WRITE ,
and a value written through the mapping reads back.
.It
The file descriptor can be passed to a child process with an
.Dv SCM_RIGHTS
message over a
.Xr socketpair 2 .
The child maps it and must see the parent's write.
The parent must then see a value written by the child.
This shows that the mapping is really shared and not copy-on-write.
.It
The object can be grown to 8192 bytes and mapped again at the new size.
The old contents must survive, and the new end must be writable.
.It
A second object can be unlinked right after it is opened, and then
still be sized, mapped and written through its file descriptor.
This is what real Wayland clients do.
.It
.Xr shm_unlink 3
removes the first name, the existing mapping keeps working, and a
second unlink of the same name fails with
.Er ENOENT .
.El
.Pp
Each check prints one line ending in
.Dq OK
or in
.Dq FAIL
with a reason.
The last line is
.Dq ALL PASS
or
.Dq FAILURES PRESENT .
.Sh FILES
.Nm
uses the shared-memory names
.Pa /wlprobe-pool
and
.Pa /wlprobe-anon .
A stale
.Pa /wlprobe-pool
from an earlier run is removed first.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 if every check passes, and 1 otherwise.
It stops early, with status 1, if the first
.Xr shm_open 3
or
.Xr mmap 2
fails, or if
.Xr socketpair 2 ,
.Xr fork 2
or
.Xr waitpid 2
fails.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr wlclient 1 ,
.Xr wlcoreprobe 1 ,
.Xr mmap 2 ,
.Xr socketpair 2 ,
.Xr shm_open 3 ,
.Xr wlcompd 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility first appeared in Ixolo 0.1.
